Here's a straightforward O(n^2) solution using a nested loop. For every start index i, we extend the end index j and count how many times two consecutive digits are equal within s[i..j]. As soon as we encounter more than one such pair, we stop expanding since the count can only increase further. The maximum length encountered is the answer.

